<!--
  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║  REFERENCE DOCUMENT — NOT passed to netconvert                      ║
  ║                                                                      ║
  ║  This file documents the 4-phase timing plan that TraCIAdapter       ║
  ║  constructs and applies to junction "C" at runtime via              ║
  ║    traci.trafficlight.setProgramLogic()                              ║
  ║                                                                      ║
  ║  Why we don't use this file in netconvert:                           ║
  ║  The <phase state="..."> string must have exactly one character per  ║
  ║  connection, in the order that netconvert assigns linkIndex values.  ║
  ║  That ordering depends on the generator's internals and cannot be    ║
  ║  predicted from the input files.  Hardcoding state strings here     ║
  ║  would produce incorrect phase assignments.                          ║
  ║                                                                      ║
  ║  Instead, generate_net.bat lets netconvert auto-generate the initial ║
  ║  traffic light program, and TraCIAdapter.build_link_map() reads the  ║
  ║  actual linkIndex values from the running simulation to construct    ║
  ║  correct state strings dynamically.                                  ║
  ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

  Design specification — 4-phase fixed-time plan, cycle = 96 s:
  ┌──────┬────────────────────────┬──────┐
  │ Phase│ Description            │  Dur │
  ├──────┼────────────────────────┼──────┤
  │  1   │ N-S Through — green    │  32s │
  │      │            — yellow   │   3s │
  │      │ All-Red                │   1s │
  ├──────┼────────────────────────┼──────┤
  │  2   │ N-S Left    — green    │  16s │
  │      │            — yellow   │   3s │
  │      │ All-Red                │   1s │
  ├──────┼────────────────────────┼──────┤
  │  3   │ E-W Through — green    │  22s │
  │      │            — yellow   │   3s │
  │      │ All-Red                │   1s │
  ├──────┼────────────────────────┼──────┤
  │  4   │ E-W Left    — green    │  10s │
  │      │            — yellow   │   3s │
  │      │ All-Red                │   1s │
  └──────┴────────────────────────┴──────┘
  Total: 4 × (green + 3 + 1) = 96 s

  Connection → movement mapping (defined in intersection.con.xml):
    N approach lane 0 → c2s  (N-S through)
    N approach lane 1 → c2e  (N left turn)
    N approach lane 0 → c2w  (N right turn — free/yield)
    S approach lane 0 → c2n  (N-S through, opposing)
    S approach lane 1 → c2w  (S left turn)
    S approach lane 0 → c2e  (S right turn — free/yield)
    E approach lane 0 → c2w  (E-W through)
    E approach lane 1 → c2s  (E left turn)
    E approach lane 0 → c2n  (E right turn — free/yield)
    W approach lane 0 → c2e  (E-W through, opposing)
    W approach lane 1 → c2n  (W left turn)
    W approach lane 0 → c2s  (W right turn — free/yield)

  State-string character codes (used by TraCIAdapter at runtime):
    G = green (protected)
    g = green (yield — right turns)
    y = yellow
    r = red

  Expected state strings once linkIndex ordering is known (see
  TraCIAdapter.build_link_map() for the runtime construction logic):
    NS_THROUGH_GREEN  : G at {N_through, S_through}, g at {right turns}
    NS_LEFT_GREEN     : G at {N_left, S_left},       g at {right turns}
    EW_THROUGH_GREEN  : G at {E_through, W_through}, g at {right turns}
    EW_LEFT_GREEN     : G at {E_left, W_left},       g at {right turns}
-->
